            "review_title": "Review at Tre Place",
            "review_text": "Life traveller\nNorth East England, United Kingdom4057 contributions\n0\nWonderful Vietnamese Restaurant on West Lake\nJul 2014 • Family\nIf you want an authentic, truly outstanding Vietnamese meal, seek out this hard to find restaurant where Vietnamese people come to celebrate special occasions. Set among clumps of huge bamboo (Tre=Bamboo in Vietnamese), there is an extensive area to sit overlooking the lake, and a beautiful, ornate wooden room prefer to eat indoors. I was taken by a Vietnamese friend, who had recently celebrated her birthday there with 20 members of her large family, and friends. We chose frog legs and squid, along with various exotic vegetables. As she said, the frog legs were like chicken, but tastier, and the squid was stuffed with delicious herbs and garlic. A Vietnamese group of singers accompanied by a Vietnamese guitar/lute player, all in traditional dress, went from table to table and played for everyone for small donations (I have them 4 x 1$ notes, which they accepted with pleasure and grace - I do find it an irony that it is the US $ which is the most sought after currency in Vietnam). My friend explained that the first song was about a young couple announcing to their parents they were both virgins and therefor ready to marry, and the next song was about a young couple whose clothes had been blown off by the wind. great stuff! This is a wonderful place which probably hasn't been found by the foreign travellers who visit Hanoi. For a great meal, with drinks, the cost was 520,000 Dong (£14.35 or $24.55). An absolute bargain and l would recommend seeking this place out unreservedly - any Hanoi taxi would take you there without any trouble whatsoever.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nWritten July 13, 2014",
